# Linux 3.10 does not apply genfscon to sysfs, so the queue attributes of the
# loop and dm devices apexd creates (read_ahead_kb, scheduler, nr_requests)
# carry the generic "sysfs" label until ueventd has handled their uevent and
# restored the sysfs_loop/sysfs_dm labels - but apexd configures them right
# after creating the device (apexd-bootstrap even runs before ueventd's
# coldboot has finished). A failed read_ahead_kb write aborts APEX activation
# and reboots the device ("bootstrap-apexd-failed").
allow apexd sysfs:file { getattr open read write };
